namespace pdg { /**

\struct pdg::SpriteTriggerEvent
\ingroup Events Animation Sprites
\brief Payload for an authored Spriter trigger delivered as eventType_SpriteTriggerEvent.

The common JavaScript payload contains:

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `emitter` | Event emitter delivering the notification |
| `eventType` | pdg::eventType_SpriteTriggerEvent |
| `actingSprite` | Sprite whose animation crossed the trigger |
| `inLayer` | SpriteLayer containing that Sprite |
| `triggerName` | Authored eventline name |
| `clipName` | Clip containing the eventline key |
| `entityName` | Spriter entity containing the clip |
| `timeSeconds` | Authored key position from clip start, in floating-point seconds |
| `offsetSeconds` | Occurrence offset from the start of the update, in floating-point seconds |

Subscribe by event type and inspect `triggerName` to distinguish authored triggers.
An `action` field is not a portable trigger discriminator. The native compatibility
field `frameTime` uses integer milliseconds and is omitted from JavaScript.
The native event ID is currently exposed by the browser bridge but not the
V8/JavaScriptCore bridges.

\sa pdg::Sprite::enableSpriterEvents
\sa pdg::eventType_SpriteTriggerEvent
\sa \ref animation_trigger_event

**/ }
